---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { facts } from "../data/site";

const hasPublicArtifact = Boolean(facts.downloadUrl);
---

<BaseLayout title="Known gaps | Downright" description="The current release, evidence, and launch gaps for the Downright site." markdownPath="/known-gaps.md" imagePath="/og/index.svg">
  <main class="subpage legal-page known-gaps-page">
    <section class="subpage-hero">
      <p class="subpage-hero__path">Downright / Known gaps</p>
      <h1>{hasPublicArtifact ? "What remains before launch." : "What is not ready yet."}</h1>
      <p>{hasPublicArtifact ? `The ${facts.version} release artifact is public. The remaining gaps below are kept visible until their own source evidence exists.` : "The implementation is verified locally. Release and native evidence gaps stay visible until their source evidence exists."}</p>
    </section>
    <article class="legal-copy">
      <h2>Release inputs</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Domain:</strong> <code>downright.cc</code> is the verified production domain, connected to Vercel through Porkbun DNS.</li>
        <li><strong>Artifact:</strong> <code>{facts.artifactName}</code> is available at {hasPublicArtifact ? <a href={facts.downloadUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">the public GitHub Release URL</a> : "no signed, notarized, stapled public URL is configured"}.</li>
        <li><strong>Homebrew:</strong> no cask is claimed until one exists and is verified.</li>
        <li><strong>Repository:</strong> <a href={facts.repository ?? "/"}>{facts.repository ?? "not configured"}</a> is the source remote; public address confirmation remains open.</li>
        <li><strong>Brand:</strong> the current knot mark ships as the canonical mark; whether it evolves before launch remains open.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Native evidence</h2>
      <p>This website intentionally publishes no screenshots. Its interactive demonstrations use live HTML, CSS, and generated document payload data. Native app verification remains a separate local release gate; the current payload follows the {facts.version} source commit <code>{facts.sourceCommit.slice(0, 7)}</code>.</p>
      <p>The approved Quick Look, Finder, conflict, density, structural zoom, theme, split view, terminal, and motion checks remain outside the website and are not represented as shipped evidence here.</p>

      <h2>Payload provenance</h2>
      <p>Native source commit <code>{facts.sourceCommit}</code>. Payload generated <code>{new Date(facts.generatedAt).toISOString()}</code>. Native working tree dirty at generation: <strong>{facts.sourceWorkingTreeDirty ? "yes; unrelated source changes were preserved" : "no"}</strong>.</p>
      <p>The technical budgets, accessibility audits, Markdown mirrors, <code>llms.txt</code>, RSS, and social OG images are generated and verified locally. The public artifact was verified on the release Mac; clean-machine download and install verification remains pending.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
